{"availability":"available","full":"kianis4/zakat-eligibility-triage-n8n","name":"zakat-eligibility-triage-n8n","description":"AI triage for zakat-eligibility review: two model calls, deterministic refusal, human-only outcomes, operational layer on n8n. Live demo linked.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-22T15:21:31Z","updated":"2026-09-03T22:28:02Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://zakat-eligibility-triage-n8n.vercel.app","topics":["ai","anthropic","human-in-the-loop","llm","n8n","nextjs","postgres","typescript","zakat"],"demo":"https://zakat-eligibility-triage-n8n.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T23:45:58.275Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T23:45:58.275Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T23:45:58.275Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:02:07.847Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-15T23:45:58.275Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This fork moves the pipeline's operational half onto n8n. Three workflows in n8n/ decide when a campaign is read, what happens when a provider fails, and who hears about it. They decide nothing about what may be said about a campaign. The original — button-driven, no orchestrator — is at kianis4/zakat-eligibility-triage and runs untouched beside this one. The reasoning is ADR-0010.","A triage agent for crowdfunding campaigns. It reads a submitted campaign, assembles the evidence a zakat determination would turn on, names what the text leaves missing or contested, and hands the file to a qualified human reviewer. It never issues a religious ruling. Every claim it makes is traceable to a span of the campaign it read, and nothing it produces is a score."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kianis4/zakat-eligibility-triage-n8n/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0b112c1210d212867ae954273d040203f41e738ca2610cbe8f3ffcdbd6ecefc6","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02